  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ if $y=\\frac{x}{cot\u2061(x)}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $cot\u2061(x)\\,+${{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | ${cot}^{2}\u2061(x)$ |",
  "worked_solution": "We calculate the derivative using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{x}{cot\u2061(x)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1(cot\u2061(x))-x(-{csc}^{2}\u2061(x))}{{cot}^{2}\u2061(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{cot\u2061(x)+x{csc}^{2}\u2061(x)}{{cot}^{2}\u2061(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
